0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hei together,\r\n\r\nI'm currently trying to setup my drone for flying inside with mocap. I tried a lot of debugging but every time the \"InvalidRequestData\" when I send data.\r\n\r\nMAVSDK version: v2.12.2-197-g6f0b1e34\r\nPX4 version: 1.15.2\r\nCompanion Computer: RPI4 (Ubuntu 22.04) \r\nConnection type: USB\r\n\r\nHere's my little code snipped:\r\n\r\n      Mocap::VisionPositionEstimate estimate;\r\n      auto now = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n      auto microseconds = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(now.time_since_epoch()).count();\r\n\r\n      estimate.position_body.x_m = 0.0f;\r\n      estimate.position_body.y_m = -0.0f;\r\n      estimate.position_body.z_m = -0.0f;\r\n      estimate.angle_body.pitch_rad = 0.0f;\r\n      estimate.angle_body.roll_rad = 0.0f;\r\n      estimate.angle_body.yaw_rad = 0.0f;\r\n      estimate.time_usec = microseconds;\r\n      estimate.pose_covariance.covariance_matrix = {0.0};\r\n      while (true)\r\n      {\r\n          result = mocap->set_vision_position_estimate(estimate);\r\n          RCLCPP_INFO(this->get_logger(), \"MAVSDK result %i\", (int)result);\r\n          std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));\r\n      }\r\n      \r\nMAVSDK can connect to the flight controller fine. Telemetry and position setpoints work also.\r\nI also tried it with the real data from the mocap system without any success. + i enabled timesync in mavsdk.\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have an idea how I can get this running? \r\nThank you very much.", "closed_by": {"login": "astro-phil", "id": 59973846, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU5OTczODQ2", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59973846?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/astro-phil", "html_url": "https://github.com/astro-phil", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/astro-phil/followers"